vm.stopPrank();\n        /////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////\n\n        ///INVESTING MANAGER FULFILLING PENDING REDEEM ORDER///////////////////\n        hoax(owner);\n        investmentVault.fulfillRedeem(user1, sharesReceivedByUser1);\n        ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////\n\n        //////USER3 REQUEST DEPOSIT/////////////////////////////////////////////\n        hoax(user3);\n        investmentVault.requestDeposit(user3Amount, user3, user3);\n        ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////\n\n        ///INVESTING MANAGER FULFILLING PENDING DEPOSIT ORDER///////////////////\n        hoax(owner);\n        investmentVault.fulfillDeposit(user3, user3Amount);\n\n        ///USER3 CLAIMING THEIR SHARE TOKENS ////////////////////////////////////\n        hoax(user3);\n        uint256 sharesReceivedByUser3=investmentVault.deposit(user3Amount, user3, user3);\n        //////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////\n\n        //Asset USER3 receives 10 times less than what USER3 should receive\n        assertEq(sharesReceivedByUser3/1e18,user3Amount/10e18); \n    \n        ///USER1 tries to withdraw tokens but it will revert with Insufficient Balance\n        uint256 investmentVaultCurrentBalance=asset.balanceOf(address(investmentVault));\n        hoax(user1);\n        vm.expectRevert(\n            abi.encodeWithSignature(\"ERC20InsufficientBalance(address,uint256,uint256)\",\n            address(investmentVault),\n            investmentVaultCurrentBalance,\n            sharesReceivedByUser1\n            ));\n        investmentVault.redeem(sharesReceivedByUser1, user1, user1);\n    }\n}\n```\n1. Add the above test code in `test/c4/POC.t.sol`\n2. Run the below command in the terminal\n```bash\nforge test --mt test_setup -vv\n```\n3. You will see output simillar to below:\n```bash\nRan 1 test for test/c4/POC.t.sol:POC\n[PASS] test_setup(